# The stop-ends-turn step: a tool result marked as a stop ends its round as
# the policy's stop does, and both stops that happen during a call's run set
# the mark. Broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail
# (docs/steps/stop-ends-turn/answered.md).

[break] the-round-ignores-a-results-stop
rule: A call whose result is marked as a stop ends the round there: no further request, and the turn ends denied.
file: crates/cineris-agent/src/round.rs
in: Round::finished
find: if let Some(reason) = turn_stop {
replace: if let Some(reason) = turn_stop.filter(|_| false) {
